{"schemaVersion":"1.0.0","kind":"eigenquestions-fine-index","destinations":[{"id":"source-question:bc6a22298fd5444af7ebdda06a5cf475a79ec96a88080b69626ff24965e8c654","title":"Which stack multiplicities and flux intersection matrices yield supersymmetric smooth-K3 compactifications, how many inequivalent realizations share those data, and can prescribed gauge groups and matter spectra be constructed directly?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0007"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:bcc6bfb083cb6ee371871bffebf1a269b65a0d96b7be7a1f77a4685c7f18e911","title":"How do quark/gluon emission and updated light-element and photon-background observations constrain the initial PBH abundance over 10^9–10^17 g? The paper also reviews constraints extending to much larger, nonevaporating PBHs.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0008"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:bc8f9ff791029aa1f4d5b1483038062c34a03094e7d025584feeeb996a451bd7","title":"Which CFTs admit useful weakly coupled holographic descriptions, and why would factorization and CFT consistency naturally lead an observer to introduce AdS fields and Witten diagrams?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0010"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:bc0a2983cdafd638eedd565441f7c58faeb0c429f6ab227bcb9923c8963055dc","title":"Can LVS constructions beyond the sequestered case satisfy dark-radiation bounds with minimal visible matter and natural parameters, especially by enhancing modulus decays into gauge bosons?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0016"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:bcb930350cfb30cb461ddebd3d55950894281611fce99b74467d22f1b7048f22","title":"Formulate higher-form global symmetries intrinsically through extended operators, and determine their consequences for selection rules, gauging, duality, spontaneous breaking, anomalies and phases of quantum field theory.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0018"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:bc10e46a1a0f84daf417b73f0bf5b9e34d339e2925a0e1d130db1551c8c2b467","title":"Can a string-inspired Kalb–Ramond torsion background generate a lepton asymmetry through tree-level heavy-Majorana-neutrino decays with only one right-handed species, supplying background-induced CP and CPT violation?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0018"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:bc93195bbce401af7ef41812ffd2c1b0a8a2348078e6007e8cb375ff37d40145","title":"Which compact-axion inflation models permit parametrically super-Planckian field ranges under the Weak Gravity Conjecture, and what additional assumptions are needed to constrain alignment models that evade the ordinary WGC?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0019"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:bc51c53219f1c1a5a6e5078fbb460cdc2045425eed0ff8fb71bdafaf1ab00035","title":"What leading thermal behavior defines the Einstein holographic regime? Thermal AdS and the neutral large black hole provide the benchmark against which the number of charged sectors is tested.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0026"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:bce375fdb00f19adb72e82094f9d2711bcd2f845630e4c929ea8ba8a934debcd","title":"Can a sum over fluctuating target-space topology reproduce the closed-string answer without beginning with the worldsheet definition? The paper uses the topological A-model on C³ as its explicit test.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0026"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:bcba3bcd39a42630e71c0606b8096790441e2f1582bc735f8e379f65f10bbaa3","title":"Can a collapsing thin-shell description supply a physical near-horizon cutoff, reproduce Bekenstein–Hawking entropy from a Dirac thermal atmosphere, and remove the species dependence when scalar and spinor contributions are combined?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0027"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:bc7d047ea7fa315802d2fdfb581f0f3d9b2678c1fd06a8868323d012c01298da","title":"Do heterotic de Sitter no-go results transfer to positive-cosmological-constant type IIB backgrounds through string dualities? The paper identifies preservation of spacetime character and correction of the duality rules as unresolved requirements.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0031"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:bc555d8572c78ed0318dd642be99e39a91c25fbf7d6bd8348d134c812ea580d4","title":"Can nonperturbative AdS/CFT establish the conjectured absence of global symmetries, completeness of internal gauge representations, and compactness of internal gauge groups, using definitions that distinguish physical symmetries from gauge redundancy?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0034"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:bc7bff207a8fc2a36917d1a6ae207475e1385d03234ecf8234f4d507af650454","title":"Can an interacting axion–dilaton system realize early dark energy that dissipates near recombination, providing a proposed mechanism for addressing the Hubble tension?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0041"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:bc7ce334a83277db2aa05625b35d73bfe5f6f1611d4e5658a858a43ecaaf7589","title":"Could a global anomaly of a specified visible-sector theory require additional infrared structure with phenomenological consequences?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0047"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:bc49f8c3bd883ef7c5a76f4bbd07a706a02c94247fd7501c381e5822061978e8","title":"Do non-toroidal compactifications and shape-modulus potentials admit analogous stabilization and relative-gradient bounds, and what replaces the toroidal coefficient 1/√p?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0047"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:bc9acb441ef20932bdb866c59e53c49267eb487cba4fbf5b25a75778bbdb85f3","title":"Does adding explicit thermal friction rescue the simplest steep exponential potential from its cold-inflation problems?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0047"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:bc8fda2450a08f2d0f91085a38cf4f9ce1c68b434e8626f52d7156f3c756975e","title":"Can exceptional field theory efficiently determine KK masses and identify the corresponding higher-dimensional fluctuations, including lower-spin sectors mixed by background fluxes, when residual isometries provide little help?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0048"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:bc2083de97790b4149a9104fd594f9041943f38c493f41f377c82e8b6795d223","title":"Do static-patch de Sitter OTOCs exhibit maximal chaos, and what do positive-energy shockwaves imply for observer complementarity and possible inflationary information exchange?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0049"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:bce9201f00e8aec9a8711df8b849314a4784db03e4a0ae3f9b02ff04f728be9d","title":"How does internal-space evolution constrain four-dimensional acceleration and Newton's constant? The reviewed construction answers this only for a compact internal metric conformally related to a specified Ricci-flat reference geometry.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0053"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:bc6be6e472bd166a34808efa4bcdd710888223f8366691104eb54788493adacd","title":"Can a classical three-form regularize a black-hole interior while leaving its low-curvature, near-horizon geometry approximately Schwarzschild? The target is an interior without the vanishing sphere radius and finite-time singularity of the vacuum solution.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0053"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:bcfcaf244290b4b08138848e28a1d9de7d4f1d97b97f8697e05e01ec37defda6","title":"How do stochastic vacuum transitions determine scalar perturbations in chain inflation? The page approaches this question through inflaton mean and variance and an illustrative construction of tunneling events and bubble-wall histories inside a past light cone.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0059"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:bcfdeed1bd17700ea33d71dbf7194b20d87c75eba1eac127e8557c76d862d22b","title":"Can omitted loops or a broader cosmological ansatz admit de Sitter solutions, and can the FRG construction be matched to string perturbation theory in critical dimension? The paper leaves these questions open and also proposes extending the approach to worldsheet Weyl-anomaly cancellation.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0062"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:bc0b5a5e9a8a08312fc1719afaee19c605238ae7eed704f6117fde41b47b38ff","title":"How can gravitational α′ corrections to closed-string effective actions be expressed through duality-invariant double field theory (DFT), and how far can gauge/Lorentz identifications systematically generate higher-derivative actions and symmetry transformations?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0067"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:bc6e2b9aed1562d87b4c7f88d5f67e810e8b281363eadc2c87958768a580f8a9","title":"Which inflationary models remain compatible with the 2021 BICEP/Keck constraints, and how do cosmological attractors accommodate small tensor amplitudes while supplying theoretically motivated B-mode targets?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0069"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:bc8b421870b960cab9d77620e76d73b4f3a6483c2f6d4f1bd40ef2e9ea4afe77","title":"Can completeness be formulated for QFT without first assuming symmetries, weak coupling or particular operators, and how does failure of completeness determine generalized symmetries and their dual partners?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0069"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:bce4035397262742d26057790846afa65311fd54f9e0de492c678b879e11a9e5","title":"This EFT tests moduli stabilization and anti-D3 uplift in a strongly warped conifold glued into a two-Kähler-modulus Calabi–Yau orientifold. It retains the conifold deformation instead of freezing the entire complex-structure sector.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0071"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:bc6d95ef304d3248650b1f725634ff597c0ab19c4aa25d2569ea9f1df310f56c","title":"The hybrid action retains metric curvature R while adding f(𝓡), where 𝓡 is built from an independent connection. The construction supplies the modified gravitational dynamics used for the inflationary application.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0075"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:bc071927d9331c7ddd7107d6c5db963468b5f8d6520573b3402d66fe8dca755a","title":"Can five-dimensional primordial black holes and a tower of massive KK gravitons provide corresponding dark-matter descriptions, both in present visible signals and in the proposed relation between black-hole accretion and graviton-gas cooling?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0077"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:bc9385604564100e2557a4af21e1349c17817ec368e165dd6bcf42